(* (⇒) Assume that ∑ a converges. series_comparison_test (see its
   statement in theories/Series.v) needs two facts, stated with ∀ n ∈ ℕ:
   - ∀ n ∈ ℕ, 0 ≤ (fun n : ℕ => a n / (1 + a n)) n, from frac_nonneg;
   - ∀ n ∈ ℕ, (fun n : ℕ => a n / (1 + a n)) n ≤ a n, from frac_le.
   Prove each as a claim. Inside, after [Take n ∈ ℕ.], get rid of the fun
   with [We need to show that 0 ≤ a n / (1 + a n).] (and similarly), and
   apply the lemma to its arguments, as in
   [By (frac_nonneg (a n) Han) we conclude that ...], where (Han) is 0 ≤ a n.
