   - By series_convergent_terms_zero, (fun n : ℕ => a n / (1 + a n)) ⟶ 0.
     Write out this limit with ε, as in Part 2, use it with ε := 1/2 and
     obtain an index N1.
   - By scaled_series_converges, the partial sums of
     sprod (fun n : ℕ => a n / (1 + a n)) 2 converge to 2 * l1.
   - Claim that the terms of this sequence are non-negative (frac_nonneg).
   - Claim that a n ≤ sprod (fun n : ℕ => a n / (1 + a n)) 2 n
     for all n > N1 (start with [Take n > N1.]): remove the absolute
